          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "**The manuscript’s cumulative BGST formula remains valid unchanged.** Substituting \\(x=T^\\alpha\\) into the **first line of v3 equation (3.5)** and dividing by \\(T\\log T/(2\\pi)\\) gives exactly\n\\[\nF_c(\\alpha,T)=T^{-2\\alpha}(\\log T+O(1))+\\alpha+O((\\log T)^{-1/2}),\n\\]\nuniformly for \\(0\\le\\alpha\\le1\\). [Corrected source, §3](https://arxiv.org/html/2501.14545v3#S3).\n\nThe erroneous **multiplicative** remainder discussed on p.7 is a different statement. The headline dyadic formula (3.2) also uses a deliberately weaker error bound.\n\nI saved the [source check and dependency audit](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/08_theta_observables_newman_dynamics/03_operator_imaginary_time_evolution/02_localized_zero_correlations/reviews/BGST_IMPORT_SOURCE_CHECK_20261108.md) and updated the reference annotations. No downstream weakening was needed within the checked scope. The parallel B04 work and all 17 frozen E03 inputs remain untouched.\n\nPrinted source checked: :codex-file-citation{path=\"/Users/Shared/szp-archive/localized-zero-correlations/references/2501.14545v3.pdf\" purpose=\"source\"}"
            ]
          },
